-- 2. a BUILTIN answers
clock_us: long
clock_us, in the subtraction: long
len: long
print: void
clock_us, painted as a builtin: builtin
len, painted as a builtin: builtin
-- 3. an f-string is sub-tokenized, not one blob
line 15: 5 spans, 26 tokens
name inside the interpolation: variable
its format spec `:`, `<`: punctuation/NO-SUCH-COLUMN
its width `14`: number
us, the second interpolation: variable
the literal ` ns/call` stays a string: string
the opening f": string
a brace: punctuation/NO-SUCH-COLUMN
print, outside the string: builtin
line 20, a plain string: 10 spans, 10 tokens
line 18, a comment: 1 spans, 1 tokens
-- 4. the language's TYPE NAMES are painted as types
long, a return type: type
str, a parameter type: type
float, a parameter type: type
P, an alias: type
a `long` that is a variable: variable
a field of a record type: variable
-- 5. a comment is ONE token, so nothing inside it is highlighted
the comment's span: comment
a bracket inside it: comment
its closing bracket agrees: comment
a paren inside it agrees too: comment/comment
#strings comes before #comments: true
at 178 and 219
the `//` in line 19's string scans as a string: string
-- 6. an IMPORTED name answers
exp of math.exp, at the call: float
e, bound from an import: ```y|float|```||```y|e|```
math itself: ```y|math|```
the import statement's own name: ```y|math|```
-- 7. completion after a `.` is the object's OWN members
math. offers 189 items: min,max,abs,clamp,sign,gcd
  the first three, and whether each has a type: min=<none>, max=<none>, abs=<none>
  string methods wrongly among them: none
z. (a record literal) offers: z
a. (a record variable) offers: a
p. (a parameter) offers: a,b
and a str offers 27 items: split,join,trim,strip,trim_start,lstrip, all of them its own
